<title>USA: Air Methods gets helicopter contract.</title>
<headline>Air Methods gets helicopter contract.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Methods Corp said early Tuesday that it has signed a 10-year with an Evansville, Ind., hospital to provide air medical transportation services.</p>
<p>Terms of the agreement with Welborn Baptist Hospital were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Welborn will switch from the Bell 206 L-1 helicopter it uses under a contract with another company to a Bell 407.</p>
<p>Air Methods also is to provide pilots and mechanics to operate the helicopter.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
